{"parentUuid":"3f6c120d-f591-4331-b29c-891f65cefd9d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"afc43fc036aaadb5a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VPvshSFsPYEvzzLxq4jgnv","type":"tool_result","content":"56-                               be specified multiple times)\n57:  --plugin-dir <path>          Load a local plugin directory (can be specified\n58-                               multiple times)\n59-  -w, --worktree [name]        Start in an isolated git worktree at\n60-                               ~/.cursor/worktrees/<reponame>/<name>. If\n--\n76-  mcp                          Manage MCP servers\n77:  plugin                       Manage plugins and plugin marketplaces\n78-  worker [options]             Run a self-hosted Cloud Agent worker that\n79-                               connects to Cursor and executes agent tool calls\n80-                               on this machine. Without --pool it is a personal\n3:Reference documentation for building, structuring, and submitting Cursor plugins. Plugins package rules, skills, agents, commands, MCP servers, and hooks into distributable bundles that work in the Cursor IDE.\n14:| Cursor Plugins                                             | `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`     | Skills, MCP servers, rules, agents, commands, hooks, variables |\n53:├── hooks/                 # Hook definitions\n54:│   └── hooks.json\n66:sections below document Cursor Plugin fields, components, and marketplace\n92:| `hooks`       | string or object         | Path to hooks config file, or inline hook config                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n116:Team admins set the actual values in the dashboard under **Plugins** (at install time, or later via **Configure** on the plugin).\n162:| Hooks       | `hooks/hooks.json`        | Parsed for hook event names                                                                |\n293:## Hooks format\n295:Hooks are automation scripts triggered by agent, Tab, or workspace events. Define them in `hooks/hooks.json`:\n297:```json title=\"hooks/hooks.json\"\n299:  \"hooks\": {\n322:- **Agent hooks**: `sessionStart`, `sessionEnd`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `postToolUseFailure`, `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `beforeShellExecution`, `afterShellExecution`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `afterMCPExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `afterFileEdit`, `beforeSubmitPrompt`, `preCompact`, `stop`, `afterAgentResponse`, `afterAgentThought`\n323:- **Tab hooks**: `beforeTabFileRead`, `afterTabFileEdit`\n324:- **App lifecycle hooks**: `workspaceOpen`\n326:For full documentation, see [Hooks](https://cursor.com/docs/hooks.md).\n349:Cursor expands `${CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT}` and `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` to the plugin's install path in `command`, `args`, `env` values, and `cwd`. It does not expand the standard's `${PLUGIN_ROOT}` and `${PLUGIN_DATA}` variables, so use `${CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT}` for the plugin root.\n398:A single Git repository can contain multiple plugins using a **marketplace manifest**. Place it at `.cursor-plugin/marketplace.json` in the repository root.\n400:### Marketplace manifest format\n404:  \"name\": \"my-marketplace\",\n427:### Marketplace manifest fields\n431:| `name`     | string | **(required)** Marketplace identifier (kebab-case)                                        |\n455:| `hooks`                                 | string or object | Path to hooks config or inline config                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n461:For a marketplace entry with `\"source\": \"my-plugin\"`:\n464:2. If found, the per-plugin manifest is merged with the marketplace entry (manifest values take precedence)\n472:│   └── marketplace.json       # Lists all plugins\n506:Go to [cursor.com/marketplace/publish](https://cursor.com/marketplace/publish) and submit your repository link.\n519:- Plugin has been tested locally\n520:- Cursor multi-plugin repositories have `.cursor-plugin/marketplace.json` at the repo root with unique plugin names","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9250262b-3463-4cc5-9d1a-fd612464e708","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:48:54.485Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3f6c120d-f591-4331-b29c-891f65cefd9d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-afc43fc036aaadb5a","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
