{"parentUuid":"d6149543-dc85-414d-9020-5c4d0a814ca1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"afc43fc036aaadb5a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffWyR9WtwTRcVrmPGBLb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `plugin-hooks` cells for codex and cursor are implemented and committed, but I haven't pushed, opened a PR or merged, because `sr-checks` hasn't finished. It was still running when I stopped, so I don't know yet whether it will refuse anything. Nothing is red that I know of. A monitor is waiting on the process.\n\nBoth cells are marked supported with deviations. The e2e tests for both mocks pass, and `go build` and `go vet` are clean.\n\n**Codex.**\n- **Recording:** the real codex ran the hooks of the enabled plugin `p1` alongside the project's own hook. The disabled `p2` and the plugin from an undeclared marketplace `p3` contributed none. The run is `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/plugin-hooks`.\n- **Mock:** it reads the plugin tables in `config.toml` and the marketplace's `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` (new file `codex-mock/internal/hooks/plugins.go`). It uses the shared `PluginContributes` check in `internal/hooks`.\n- **Test:** the e2e test replays the recording and also checks the two negative cases.\n- **Deviations (modeled-surface):** no install into codex's plugin cache, no git marketplaces, no hooks entry in the plugin manifest, no `PLUGIN_ROOT`/`PLUGIN_DATA` variables, no trust review.\n\n**Cursor.**\n- **Recording:** a plugin directory loaded with `--plugin-dir` ran its hook alongside the project's, and the unloaded `p2` did not. The run is `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/plugin-hooks`.\n- **Mock:** it gains a `--plugin-dir` flag and loads those plugins' hooks (new file `cursor-mock/internal/hooks/plugin.go`).\n- **Test:** the e2e test replays the recording.\n- **Deviation (capability-grounding):** Cursor has no settings file that declares a marketplace or enables a plugin, and the marketplace commands can't be driven headlessly. So the recording shows only a directly loaded plugin, not marketplace resolution.\n- **Deviation (modeled-surface):** the mock doesn't read marketplace manifests or an inline hooks object in a plugin manifest.\n\n**Shared files I had to touch.**\n- Both `capture.sh` scripts gain an optional `setup/prepare.sh`. Other agents may add the same thing, so a merge conflict is possible there.\n- `cursor-mock/internal/runner/run.go` carries other capabilities' markers. I changed one line there (passing the plugin directories to `hooks.Load`), so the judges may re-judge those pairs.\n- In the codex tests, `helpers_test.go` gained a `HomeFiles` field, and `Files` entries now create parent directories.\n- In the cursor tests, `replay_test.go` gained `replayWith`, which runs the scenario's `prepare.sh` and passes extra arguments to the mock.\n\nI also froze three doc pages into the MANIFESTs: the codex plugins page and the two cursor plugin pages. The commit is rebased on `origin/main`, with the spec cells in `spec/capabilities/plugin-hooks.yaml`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":179752,"output_tokens":1091,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":343},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1091,"cache_read_input_tokens":179752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":343,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffWyQrQwf1nuo1sBUTC8","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e93e502-ec4f-4d5c-945f-ed03f89c1e05","timesta