{"parentUuid":"5aceaff6-cc32-4c76-941d-680cf657bf7d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"afc43fc036aaadb5a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffhAbeGMPpLyu8KNwUkN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have not pushed, opened a PR or merged. The `verify-before-push` gate still refuses, on one pair: `noninteractive-run/cursor`.\n\n- **Result:** the `sr-checks` run on exactly the gate's range (base `bf1f4613`, head `7b157ae3`, rebased on #111) has one refusal. `plugin-hooks` passes, and the grounded and rigor judges for it are green.\n- **The refusal:** the headless doc says print mode without `--force` only proposes file changes. The mock accepts and ignores `--force`/`--yolo` with no declared deviation and no test. The doc's write/read tool-call frame shapes are also unchecked.\n- **Why my change is judged on it:** `Run` in `cursor-mock/internal/runner/run.go` carries the `sr:provides noninteractive-run/cursor` marker. My edit there is one line, so the pair is judged on my changeset. The line is `hooks.Load(cfg.Dir, cfg.PluginDirs...)`, which is how the `--plugin-dir` hooks reach the mock.\n- **Ownership:** this is the gap your `noninteractive-run` debt agent is fixing. I haven't tried to fix it, and nothing has landed on `origin/main` yet.\n\n**Open choices:**\n1. I wait until the `noninteractive-run` fix lands, then rebase, re-run `sr-checks` on that range, push, open the PR and admin-merge once CI passes.\n2. I avoid editing `Run`. The only way I can see is a package-level setter for the plugin dirs, which breaks the config-at-entry rule, so I'd rather not.\n\nI'm leaning towards (1) unless you tell me otherwise. Everything is committed locally on top of `origin/main` at `bf1f4613`: the two codex and cursor recordings, the cells, the adapters and the tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_inpu