{"parentUuid":"36f44f0d-9a5f-4a2b-9c5b-e2d81577fc2c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"afc43fc036aaadb5a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqvqbZo4Yv9VJnfvoTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both `plugin-hooks` cells are now supported, and PR #131 is merged. Every CI check passed first, and `sr-checks` on the gate's base and head came back clean with no refusals.\n\n**codex: supported.** I recorded the real codex with a local marketplace `mk`: `p1` enabled, `p2` disabled, and `p3` enabled under a marketplace that was never declared.\n- **Recording:** only `p1`'s hook and the project's own ran, in `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/plugin-hooks`.\n- **Adapter:** the mock reads the plugin tables in `config.toml` and the marketplace's `marketplace.json`, using the shared `PluginContributes` core (`codex-mock/internal/hooks/plugins.go`).\n- **Test:** the e2e replay also checks the undeclared-marketplace and disabled-plugin cases.\n- **Deviations (modeled-surface):**\n  - no plugin install into codex's cache\n  - no git marketplaces\n  - no `hooks` entry in the plugin manifest\n  - no `PLUGIN_ROOT`/`PLUGIN_DATA` variables\n  - no trust review\n\n**cursor: supported.** I recorded the real `cursor-agent` loading a plugin directory with `--plugin-dir`. Its hook ran alongside the project's, and the unloaded `p2` did not, in `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/plugin-hooks`.\n- **Adapter:** the mock gains a `--plugin-dir` flag (`cursor-mock/internal/hooks/plugin.go`).\n- **Tests:** an e2e replay, plus a unit test for default and manifest-named hooks discovery.\n- **Deviation (capability-grounding):** cursor has no settings file that declares a marketplace or enables a plugin; marketplaces and enablement live on the account side. So the recording shows a directly loaded plugin, not marketplace resolution.\n- **Deviation (modeled-surface):** the mock doesn't read marketplace manifests or an inline hooks object.\n\n**Shared files I edited:** both `capture.sh` scripts gain an optional `setup/prepare.sh`, and the codex and cursor e2e helpers each gained a small addition. I also froze three doc pages into the MANIFESTs. I edited one line inside `Run` in `cursor-mock/internal/runner/run.go`, which is the only edit on a marked declaration. By merge time it raised no refusal.\n\nNothing is left red."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":219,"cache_read_input_tokens":249965,"output_tokens":839,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":219},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":249965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":219,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":219,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffqvpowJ1ksYj6SneE3g","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ac566a6c-3610-4bd3-811a-3f10ab73ca79","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:19:43.865Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-afc43fc036aaadb5a","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a8a444ee54a52b4dc"}
